# Line endings are pinned, not normalised.
#
# This repo is genuinely mixed and that is fine: the files Windows tools read
# are CRLF, the files bash and WSL read are LF. What is NOT fine is git
# rewriting them on checkout, because both halves break in ways that are hard
# to see:
#
#   a .sh or .zsh file with CRLF  -> bash reports "command not found" on a
#                                    line that looks correct
#   a .cmd file with LF           -> cmd.exe can mis-handle multi-line
#                                    if/else blocks
#   a BOM on anything WSL reads   -> "<BOM>printf: command not found"
#
# So: no automatic conversion anywhere, then force the endings that matter.
* -text

# --- must be LF: read by bash, zsh, or WSL ----------------------------------
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.zsh       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
zshrc       text eol=lf
aliases.zsh text eol=lf
gitconfig   text eol=lf
.wslconfig  text eol=lf

# --- must be CRLF: read by cmd.exe ------------------------------------------
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# --- GitHub language stats --------------------------------------------------
# Without this the repo reads as mostly "Rich Text Format" or similar, because
# .tmpl and config files outweigh the code.
*.tmpl      linguist-language=TOML
docs/**     linguist-documentation
